# CHERRYAIL Project Ops

Operational guardrails inspired by CHERRY project rules.

## Modular Discipline

- Keep files focused and small.
- If a file grows beyond ~300 lines and responsibilities diverge, split before adding more.
- Prefer one responsibility per module and clear file naming by behavior.

## Change Tracking

For non-trivial features:
- Maintain a short feature note (scope, files, rationale, current status).
- Append dated changelog bullets for material updates.
- Keep progress honest; if regressions are found, lower status and document why.

## Cross-Platform Care

- Verify behavior on Windows/macOS/Linux-sensitive paths, shell commands, and filesystem assumptions.
- Avoid platform-specific shortcuts unless guarded.

## Comment Policy

- Comment only non-obvious intent and tradeoffs.
- Avoid narration comments.

## Safety Baseline

- No silent fallback that hides critical failures.
- Prefer explicit error messages and actionable recovery paths.

